{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts","id":1370965,"title":"What is the best combination of three Martial Arts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-28T03:02:39-08:00","id":1370965,"title":"What is the best combination of three Martial Arts?","content":"Or alternatively, 2 Martial Arts and an Evocation tree. <br /> <br /> What do I mean by best? <br /> Most powerful? Coolest? Most fun? Most straightforward (combining 30 charms is complex)? Best at dealing with a wide variety of situations, including non-combat? Well, that's up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T13:40:41-08:00","id":1371081,"title":"","content":"I'll propose an entry for &quot;Most Confusing&quot;:<br /> Black Claw Style, Righteous Devil Style, and a set of Silken Armor with evocations that make it very difficult to fight you outside a duel. <br /> You: &quot;I am Paradoxical Blossom, here to rid this city of the filth that lurks the alleys! Show your mettle, scum!&quot;<br /> Foe: &quot;Fine then, I'll take you on!&quot;<br /> You: &quot;Dragons preserve me, this man is <i>trying to kill me for no reason</i>!&quot;<br /> Foe: &quot;What? You just challenged me to a duel!&quot;<br /> You: &quot;Yes, for I am an upright and honorable warrior here to punish you!&quot;<br /> Foe: &quot;But then-&quot;<br /> You: &quot;<i>And I have been so cruelly and viciously set upon!</i>&quot;<br /> Foe: &quot;Uh, guys? Back me up here?&quot;<br /> Guys: &quot;No way boss, we're not intruding in a duel you agreed to and started for no reas- huh? Uhhhh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T14:05:29-08:00","id":1371084,"title":"","content":"My sidereal just might have a new method of fighting now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T14:42:36-08:00","id":1371091,"title":"","content":"First, an Evocation-Duel tree with Black Claw Style and Righteous Devil Style is hilarious.<br /> <br /> Minor aside for a pet peeve. To claim something as 'best' with a defined criteria for ranking, one must rank all possibilities. Ignoring Evocations, and ignoring books that aren't 3e Core, 3e Lunars, and 3e Dragon-Blooded, there's 20 styles. 20 choose 3 is 1140. Without a defined criteria for ranking, well, it's a lost cause. However, I'll take off my analytical hat, and enjoy the writing prompt.<br /> <br /> Falcon/Air/White Reaper<br /> Pros: <br /> Light-armor compatible<br /> Flying-friendly<br /> Head-butts are shockingly good at approximating weapons of mass destruction vs. battlegroups<br /> <br /> Cons:<br /> Hard to get onslaught penalties in the air<br /> Form weapons don't line up<br /> Does not come with wings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T14:56:17-08:00","id":1371092,"title":"","content":"Fists are form weapons!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T00:50:08-08:00","id":1371205,"title":"","content":"I have a few ideas of at least interesting combinations, but this is actually how I've designed Perfected Kata Bracers for the games I'm in.<br /> <br /> I take three Martial Arts styles that at least share a form weapon between them, then build on them with interlaced charm trees; a 5-7 Evocation tree for each combination, and then generally another set of very powerful charms for all three combined together. I found that using three Martial Arts let you focus on the parts where the thematics overlapped effectively and to pull out interesting combinations of the unique mechanics without ruining the entire point of investing in a Martial Arts style. Rather then covering for weaknesses where the styles still offered nothing, it boosted the strengths inherent in combining them, attempting to combine them into a single being.<br /> <br /> Another major part of this was the Style Points system from 2E's Cobra style. Leaning into how your martial arts function together, changing between them to get the drop on your opponent when you identify a moment where one is more beneficial, etc, result in building style points that you can use to reset the charms in the styles, to reduce Wound Penalties to keep fighting, or to reroll dice from failed rolls in the abilities those Martial Arts build on. The intent is to basically make it so that, while you might not be able to learn past the styles themselves, through the bracers you can expand what you're good at and, for very long running games, maybe even continue to expand on the style.<br /> <br /> I did this for Black Claw, White Veil, and Ebon Shadow, and then another one for Fire Dragon, Steel Devil, and Snake Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T07:47:17-08:00","id":1371974,"title":"","content":"Tiger/Ebon Shadow/Frost Thorn Knuckles<br /> <br /> Ideally paired with Solar Athletics (Foe Vaulting Method and Thunderbolt Attack Prana) and Stealth (Blinding Battle Feint) and with the Pain Tolerance merit (because who doesn't like having all their health levels as -0 levels?).<br /> <br /> Essence 1 (no Mastery or Solar Charms): Enter Stealth (using Nothing But Shadows if required) and assume Ebon Shadow Form. If possible, alpha strike with Glacial Beast Claw: you reset to 6i and can Reflexively switch to Tiger form. Seven Points of Weakness for Light/Medium armor or Striking Fury Claws for Heavy on Withering attacks, to build back up.<br /> <br /> I feel like Earth Dragon Style would combo well -- Force of the Mountain is a very modest dip for double 10s on Decisives (Earth Dragon Form and Perfection of Earth Body being fantastic for a Tiger Stylist with Frost Thorn Knuckles, even if not a Deeb). Water Dragon Style is very &quot;meh&quot; for this combo for Celestials, but with Aura (and the ability to ignore the Terrestrial keyword) it's a brilliant bolt-on for Deebs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1371081#post1371081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll propose an entry for &amp;quot;Most Confusing&amp;quot;:<br /> Black Claw Style, Righteous Devil Style, and a set of Silken Armor with evocations that make it very difficult to fight you outside a duel. </div> </div> </div> </div>IDK. They don't share a Form weapon.<br /> <br /> Open Palm Caress: Only works if you don't win Join Battle. No form weapon for Mastery effect.<br /> <br /> Torn Lotus Defense: Backbone of the build. Works perfectly.<br /> <br /> Flexing the Emerald Claw: No Form weapon.<br /> <br /> Black Claw Form: So useful to a Righteous Devil. Arguably better than Righteous Devil Form.<br /> <br /> Doe Eyes Defense: Works fine.<br /> <br /> Storm Calming Embrace: No Form weapon.<br /> <br /> Table Turning Reversal: No Form weapon. And Righteous Devil does it better.<br /> <br /> Outrage Kindling Cry: Oh so deliciously good... <br /> <br /> Heart Ripping Claw: Again, no Form weapon.<br /> <br /> There's a really cool theme here, but it's mechanically shaky. (Totally showing this to my ST though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-29-2020, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T08:07:48-08:00","id":1371978,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I don't get the business about Pain Tolerance? That just lowers -2s to -1s, and -4 to -3? I mean, it's a good merit, but I assume you said it because there's some synergy I'm missing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T08:29:39-08:00","id":1371983,"title":"","content":"Anyone have a recommendation for DBs? I'm particularly interested to see if anyone has any ideas that aren't all about Immaculate Dragon Styles.<br /> <br /> My friend uses Snake/Air Dragon/Crane. There's some interesting stuff going on, but they don't seem to gel perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T08:51:11-08:00","id":1371987,"title":"","content":"For DBs I like much Water Dragon Style and Crane Style, activating the Crane Form and using the Water Dragon's first charm, you can make an attack, make a full defense and still making Counterattacks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T09:43:10-08:00","id":1371992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1371978#post1371978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. I don't get the business about Pain Tolerance? That just lowers -2s to -1s, and -4 to -3? I mean, it's a good merit, but I assume you said it because there's some synergy I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Evocations of the Frost-Thorn Knuckles<br /> When attuned [...] she awakens Rimebound Predator Endurance at no cost.<br /> <br /> Rimebound Predator Endurance<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Drawing on a hunting beast\u2019s tenacity, the wielder numbs herself to cold and pain. If she has Survival 4+ or a Survival specialty that relates to frigid environs, she also ignores one point of wound penalty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1371983#post1371983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have a recommendation for DBs? I'm particularly interested to see if anyone has any ideas that aren't all about Immaculate Dragon Styles.<br /> <br /> My friend uses Snake/Air Dragon/Crane. There's some interesting stuff going on, but they don't seem to gel perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1368113#post1368113\">Single Point Shining Into the Void/Water Dragon/Stormcaller</a> worked surprisingly well.<br /> <br /> Water Dragon is going to combo basically with everything because Become The Hammer means you can enter Water Aura every turn (congratulations you're no longer bound by the Terrestrial Keyword). Tiger Claws are a pretty common Form weapon as an added bonus. (Crane/Water Dragon looks amazing.)<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon is pretty fantastic too -- compatible with all armor, but also containing non-armor defensive options. You'll want to use Force of the Mountain on every attack (and at 3m, it's under your mote regen) so Aura isn't much of an issue. Form weapon is an issue -- you're going unarmed with this one. Good synergy with Tiger style -- knock foes prone, get +3 Charm dice to attack them, they spend Initiative to try to stand back up.<br /> <br /> I feel like there should be a Righteous Devil/Wood Dragon(/White Reaper?) combo, but I can't <i>quite </i>put it together (lots of damage boosters and helpful ancillary effects, no stratagey beyond &quot;spend a lot of motes&quot;)... Likewise Air Dragon/Ebon Shadow(/White Veil?) seems like it <i>should </i>work. The main problem is managing Aura, but fighting with the Terrestrial Keyword/out of Aura shouldn't be <i>too </i>crippling.<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon/Steel Devil... I don't see. I know it's the &quot;go to&quot; combo but holy hill -- have you looked at those mote costs? Native Melee is half the Charms at half the motes, with easier Aura. I think this is a trap option. (DrLoveMonkey posted a great defense of this combo though so... IDK.)<br /> <br /> I'm surprised Snake/Air/Crane don't gel. Crane is good for Deebs, even with the Terrestrial keyword. Air is a solid ultility suite with Onslaught negation (that combos well with Snake). Snake is... awkward with the Terrestrial keyword... and remains awkward even expending Aura (as it only gives you 1 Tick's grace, and generating Air Aura is a pain -- I'm guessing your friend uses Soaring Leap Technique a lot to position?)... but Reflexive Clash (Snake Strikes the Heel) and post roll defence (Serpentine Evasion/Countless Coils Evasion) seem like they should be a godsend to Crane stylists. You need Dodge.<br /> <br /> Going completely away from Immaculate Styles... Black Claw/White Veil/Dreaming Pearl?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-29-2020, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T10:44:36-08:00","id":1371995,"title":"","content":"So, technically Rainwalker isn\u2019t a form weapon for Crane style.... but, once you get it set up, you can set it floating in the air around you and pull out your fans or hook swords or something. And it gives further boosts to taking full defense actions which Crane really likes. Are there any other counterattack focused styles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T11:30:19-08:00","id":1372001,"title":"","content":"What made you think of Righteous Devil/Wood Dragon? I'd expect it to be combined with other staff styles; so that is White Reaper, Golden Janissary and Laughing Monster, I think.<br /> <br /> Was your idea to use Righteous Devil to attack and Wood Dragon to defend?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T12:47:07-08:00","id":1372021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1372001#post1372001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What made you think of Righteous Devil/Wood Dragon? I'd expect it to be combined with other staff styles; so that is White Reaper, Golden Janissary and Laughing Monster, I think.<br /> <br /> Was your idea to use Righteous Devil to attack and Wood Dragon to defend?</div> </div> </div> </div>Righteous Devil Form lets you use your gun as a staff and lets you use many RD Charms with said gunstaff, so by combining the 2 you get Wood Dragon but with a gunstaff instead of a bowstaff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T12:59:14-08:00","id":1372022,"title":"","content":"It counts as a staff? Hmmm, now that is interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T15:56:25-08:00","id":1372047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1372022#post1372022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It counts as a staff? Hmmm, now that is interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This only applies while in Righteous Devil Form, it seems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Righteous Devil Form</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, while in this form, the Righteous Devil can use firewands effectively in close combat, using the butt or handle of a flame weapon to effectively bludgeon enemies. When used in this way, they are treated as medium weapon with the bashing, martial arts, and shield tags. Firewands with an affixed bayonet instead have the lethal tag. While this use is not compatible with effects that specifically modify ranged attacks, such as the range extension of Blossom of Inevitable Demise, it can still benefit from other Charms of this or other staff or spear-compatible styles</div> </div> </div> </div>Firewands are also said to be treated as a short spear when affixed with a bayonet in their write-up in Chapter 9.<br /> <br /> Edit: Herp derp, I should have better reading comprehension. Didn't see that this was already pointed out in Epitome's post about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24959-mynorin","user":"Mynorin","date":". 02-29-2020, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24959-mynorin","name":"Mynorin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T17:29:43-08:00","id":1372061,"title":"","content":"Having looked at it I see what you mean JohnDoe: you can use Wood Dragon and Righteous Devil, but the fact you can't apply the offensive charms from both makes it a little pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T20:58:12-08:00","id":1372093,"title":"","content":"I just like the idea of Black Claw and Laughing Monster to utterly ruin your opponents' concept of friend and foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T23:38:45-08:00","id":1372102,"title":"","content":"Two I can get you (from my build perambulation) three is madness, unless you are only dipping the third, you're going to be spread awfully thin on a group of charms that all equate to &quot;Punch Stuff Good&quot;.<br /> <br /> So my off the top of my head picks for Two MAs w/good synergy:<br /> <br /> Tiger and Ebon Shadow: The classic stealthy tiger approach, shares a form weapon. Absolutely horrendous alpha strikes start of combat that can lead into reflexive form activation that can lead into continually resetting into 10 dice decisives, a classic.<br /> <br /> Black Claw and Dreaming Pearl Courtesan: For a socially focused MAist - Black Claw provides the damaging oomph and DPC provides defenses. Pretty decent synergy.<br /> <br /> Black Claw and White Veil: As above, but focused around amping up the poison of Black Claw, the poison of wood dragon's claw (w/ Spring Razor's Evocations, a good thematic fit) and making people second guess if you actually attacked them while bleeding (internally) from a (hah) broken heart. Admittedly, less soak, so you better get your Doe Eyes Defence penalty maxxed.<br /> <br /> Snake and Ebon Shadow: Both dex based so decent synergy there. The money combo is Seven Points of Weakness Strike (Ebon Shadow) + Armor Penetrating Fang Strike (Snake) + Foe Vaulting Attack (Athletics) to give yourself a guaranteed +10 dice to post soak withering damage.<br /> <br /> Hmm, if I can remember more I'll be sure to tack them on here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 03-01-2020, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T00:43:48-08:00","id":1372107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1372061#post1372061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having looked at it I see what you mean JohnDoe: you can use Wood Dragon and Righteous Devil, but the fact you can't apply the offensive charms from both makes it a little pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the wording on RDF specifies &quot;<b>the range extension</b> of Blossom of Inevitabile Demise&quot;, so I think ALL the damage boosters from RDS except Azure Abacus should stack with Wood Dragon. Which is a lot of Withering damage. Plus Wood Dragon healing. Plus pure Righteous Devil as foes run away. Plus Righteous Devil gives the reloading and range extension that Deebs struggle with on Firewands.<br /> <br /> Is it better than using a bow with native Archery and Wood Dragon? Probably not. But Righteous Devil combos well with Performance, and is probably the only viable way of using flame weapons on a Deeb without custom Charms or Sekhem. Not that Sekhem hurts the combo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T01:31:39-08:00","id":1372111,"title":"","content":"Thinking about firewands (and Dragon-Sigh Wands), bayonets count as short spears. Could Righteous Devil be combined with White Reaper or Golden Jannisary for defence and the occasional decisive attack (to save reloading, since the main benefit of flame weapons is Withering damage)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T02:30:19-08:00","id":1372118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1372111#post1372111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about firewands (and Dragon-Sigh Wands), bayonets count as short spears. Could Righteous Devil be combined with White Reaper or Golden Jannisary for defence and the occasional decisive attack (to save reloading, since the main benefit of flame weapons is Withering damage)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd hope so, because I've done RD/WR using exactly that synergy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T03:12:05-08:00","id":1372121,"title":"","content":"How'd it go?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T05:23:59-08:00","id":1372134,"title":"","content":"Combine Silvertongue Nightengale Style with Celestial Monkey style<br /> <br /> How you can shout people in the nuts for extra damage. (provided that they have valor as their main virtue)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T06:07:38-08:00","id":1372139,"title":"","content":"Celestial Monkey Style hasn't been converted to 3e yet, and Virtues aren't a thing in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T06:14:30-08:00","id":1372141,"title":"","content":"I've seen someone suggest Black Claw/Mantis Style, so add in another martial art of artifact that boosts grapples and/or poisons<br /> Core charms are Flexing the Emerald Claw, Storm-Calming Embrace and Joint-Locking Technique for an indefinite grapple while they slowly die.<br /> <br /> Black Claw/White Veil/Falcon or Dreaming Pearl - &quot;We aren't fighting, if we are they started it, and if it's my fault can you blame me when I look this good?&quot;<br /> <br /> Silver Voiced Nightingale/Swaying Grass Style/Dreaming Pearl Courtesan for mastering as many forms of dance-fighting as possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T21:39:46-08:00","id":1372377,"title":"","content":"I once saw a hilarious solar Ebon Shadow/Tiger/White Veil build based around just murdering people at a party by using Ebon Shadow and White Veil's stealth enchancers and TAP to deal like 65 levels of lethal damage, and then reflexively using hidden snake recoil to dissapear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25732-wrecksalot","name":"wrecksalot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T22:25:57-08:00","id":1372385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1372107#post1372107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually the wording on RDF specifies &quot;<b>the range extension</b> of Blossom of Inevitabile Demise&quot;, so I think ALL the damage boosters from RDS except Azure Abacus should stack with Wood Dragon. Which is a lot of Withering damage. Plus Wood Dragon healing. Plus pure Righteous Devil as foes run away. Plus Righteous Devil gives the reloading and range extension that Deebs struggle with on Firewands.<br /> <br /> Is it better than using a bow with native Archery and Wood Dragon? Probably not. But Righteous Devil combos well with Performance, and is probably the only viable way of using flame weapons on a Deeb without custom Charms or Sekhem. Not that Sekhem hurts the combo.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording is &quot;While this use is not compatible with effects that specifically modify ranged attacks,&quot; and then gives blossom as an example. That'd be any charm that affects the flame discharge (blossom, azure abacus, etc) since even at close range band that's still a ranged attack, like with thrown or archery. Kiss of the sun, on the other hand, supplements an Aim action, so that'd play nice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T06:12:51-08:00","id":1372439,"title":"","content":"<s>Not saying I agree with Vance, but that's not what Vance said:</s><br /> <br /> Edit: Vance and I agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1372432#post1372432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Righteous Devil Charms that can enhance hand-to-hand attacks are Blossom of Inevitable Death (only the double 10s on damage part), Kiss of the Sun Concentration, Azure Abacus Meditation, Phoenix Flies on Golden Wings, and Caress of 1000 Hells.<br /> <br /> (If you have trouble visualizing how Caress of 1000 Hells works when walloping someone, it probably involves discharging the fire wand and causing the flames to wreathe the striking bit.)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-04-2020, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T09:51:33-08:00","id":1372491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1372439#post1372439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not saying I agree with Vance, but that's not what Vance said:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was in fact wrong; shouldn't answer questions before I've had my coffee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T12:28:22-08:00","id":1372511,"title":"","content":"Wood Dragon plus Golden Janissary against a spirit who is also a Creature of Darkness is pretty great. A demon hunting monk would love that combo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T13:54:59-08:00","id":1372537,"title":"","content":"Personal Favorite is Silver-Voiced Nightingale/Laughing Monster/Swaying Grass Dance, it's great for a trickster martial artist that isn't into the demonicness of Black Claw.<br /> <br /> Jubilant Battle Proposition lets you reflexively activate Nightingale Form of your join-battle, then you can reflexively slip into Laughing Monster Form after someone attacks you and you defend with the evasion bonus from Nightingale Form, so you don't have to worry about not geting your form up.<br /> <br /> Using your Voice of the Night Bird 'weapon' for withering attacks that you can flurry with influence, and Laughing Monster for unarmed decisive counter-attacks and gambits, you have incredible action economy.<br /> <br /> You can use the reflexive influence rolls from Laughing Nightingale to give people negative intimacies toward you for Deeper-Into-Trouble.<br /> <br /> Hearing the Hearts Song (with the Master effect) has incredible synergy with Laughing Monster Form. With socialize charms you can steal 15+ initiative, which on top of the 3 lost for missing a decisive lets you counterattack for ~20 decisive without reseting to base (or spending the initiative you stole).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T22:32:51-08:00","id":1372624,"title":"","content":"May I suggest an 'unofficial' Style called 'Man, Made Missile' Style. All it is is using existing Brawl,Thrown,and Athletics with the understanding of<i> &quot;There is no difference between my enemy and my ammunition.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> Artifacts that help with Feats of Strength and grappling, give bonuses to improvised weapons, and grant the thrown quality to improvised weapons or people you are grappling, would be helpful.<br /> <br /> This is a great way to chew the scene and get stunt bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T00:51:28-08:00","id":1372633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1372491#post1372491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was in fact wrong; shouldn't answer questions before I've had my coffee.</div> </div> </div> </div>Editted, appreciate the clarification. Thanks for your time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T02:17:41-07:00","id":1412975,"title":"","content":"So this is foul necromancy and I should probably wait to bring this thread back untill we get some new MAs with Many Faced Strangers but this combo is too fun.<br /> <br /> Solar Dodge to Seven Shadow Evasion<br /> Laughing Monster to the Form charm<br /> Crane to Mournfull Cranes Cry<br /> <br /> Someone attacks you with a doomcombo, you activate SSE and they lose initiative thanks to its prereqs., letting you activate Laughing Monster Form which triggers a decisive counterattack with a war fan (that doesn't reset you to base initiative) that you can enhance with Mournfull Cranes Cry to bounce the doomcombo back at the attacker.<br /> <br /> Single Point stylist goes splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 09-11-2020, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T03:17:31-07:00","id":1412978,"title":"","content":"Can you use your Form-granted counterattack against an attack that processed before the Form was active though?<br /> <br /> Probably better to enter the Form by pissing them off enough that they take a swing at you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T03:40:07-07:00","id":1412983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1412978#post1412978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use your Form-granted counterattack against an attack that processed before the Form was active though?<br /> <br /> Probably better to enter the Form by pissing them off enough that they take a swing at you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean Crane Style specifically tells you you can, but you might also read this to only mean Crane Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T06:18:44-07:00","id":1412999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370965-what-is-the-best-combination-of-three-martial-arts?p=1371983#post1371983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have a recommendation for DBs? I'm particularly interested to see if anyone has any ideas that aren't all about Immaculate Dragon Styles.<br /> <br /> My friend uses Snake/Air Dragon/Crane. There's some interesting stuff going on, but they don't seem to gel perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, another Immaculate style one, but as this thread has come up again thought I'd add this that has proven the most fun we've had MA combos and the Divine Heritage merit: we have a fae-blooded DB NPC (recruiter for the Cult of Violet Fangs) in our game who combines Water Dragon and Snake with the the Soul-Thieving Method Eclipse charm from the Doppelganger from <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/212466/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Doppleganger-and-MataYadh-Demon\" target=\"_blank\">HDNP</a>.<br /> <br /> Combo-ing Armour-Penetrating Fang Strike with STM and Theft-Of-Essence Method and then using Essence-Dousing Wave Attack to nix form was hella WP intensive but shut down our PC Earth Dragon user, was a real &quot;Sit DOWN boy, the grown-ups are talking&quot; moment. Not an optimal combo I don't think, but felt very characterful.<br /> <br /> Anyone else done anything fun with MAs and Eclipse charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 09-11-2020, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}